\f1 \b0 \fs28 \pard \s3 \li1512 \fi0 \ri1007 \ql \tx3603 \tx3981 \tx4359 An NSTableColumn stores the display characteristics and attribute identifier\i  \i0 for a column in an NSTableView. The NSTableColumn determines the width and width limits, resizability, and editability of its column in the NSTableView. It also stores two NSCell objects: the \i header cell\i0 , which is used to draw the column header, and the \i data cell\i0 , used to draw the values for each row. You can control the display of the column by setting the subclasses of NSCell used and by setting the font and other display characteristics for these NSCells. For example, you can use the default NSTextFieldCell for displaying string values or substitute an NSImageCell to display pictures.\
\fs14\
\fs28 See the NSTableView class specification for a general overview.\
\fs14\
